 @{id='01-broadcast';name='Live Broadcast';style='Premium live sports broadcast art direction. Very dark espresso black, warm white, luminous restrained vermilion, soft gray. Cinematic wide video occupies upper-middle 65 percent of canvas, framed with professional editorial broadcast lower-third exercise title, NOT text over athlete. An asymmetrical oversized score bug floats to LEFT of video in dedicated solid black area: huge 9, small target, minus and plus. A precise four-row set rundown is on RIGHT of video as broadcast schedule. Entire lower quarter is a beautifully designed control desk: weight stepper left, 3 large numeric metrics center, horizontal bar motion ruler right, finish action at bottom right. Beautiful typographic contrast, tiny live status dot, large negative spaces, purposeful cropping of background graphic only. Not neon gaming, not slanted racing panels. Motion concept: score numeral rolls vertically, progress line sweeps gently.'},
 @{id='02-spatial';name='Spatial Flow';style='Sophisticated spatial computing sports interface: deep midnight blue background with soft blurred cobalt and violet ambient light ONLY in background, clean high contrast glass panels, physically subtle translucency, generous layered depth, no illegible text. CENTRAL nearly square athlete video panel, LEFT a floating sculptural solid circular progress dial around large 9 with distinct minus and plus below; RIGHT a slender beautifully spaced vertical workout set list, 4 rows. Across BOTTOM a single elevated rounded control tray with weight stepper, three metrics, compact horizontal position instrument and finish button. Exercise title top left. Clear separation between video and controls. Elegant highly polished native spatial OS design, not cheap sci-fi HUD. Motion concept: current motion marker follows movement softly; controls remain still.'},
 @{id='03-rhythm';name='Movement Rhythm';style='New rhythm-driven information design. Warm bone white background, deep ink typography, vivid ultramarine accent, coral for current position, red emergency stop. A broad clean HORIZONTAL MOTION TRACK runs through the CENTER of the screen, bounded at 640 and 1320 with current 980 marker and a subtle trailing wave representing movement history; no fake ECG or made-up measurements. ABOVE track: giant editorial 9 on left with minus/plus and goal, beautiful landscape video on right. BELOW track: four discrete set milestones as clean flat numbered row, separate weight stepper left and three very readable metric blocks across right. Generous whitespace, Swiss grid, striking typographic hierarchy, no dashboard card clutter, no angular racing graphics. Finish and skip in bottom action row. Motion concept: marker glides with measured bar motion; rep count updates only at completion.'},
 @{id='04-editorial';name='Athletic Editorial';style='Radical contemporary sports editorial poster turned into functional UI. Warm off-white canvas and carbon black typography, rich burgundy #7f183a, selective acid-yellow accent occupying under 8 percent only. Giant custom condensed numeral 9 at UPPER LEFT with clearly positioned minus plus, exercise title in bold editorial type to its right. LOWER LEFT a big video cropped only to frame, full athlete visible, inset fine caption. RIGHT HALF a strong vertical composition: four-set timeline with big round numbered milestones and thin connector; weight stepper as a wide inset control below; three metrics in a neat unboxed type row. Bar position as narrow vertical ruler BETWEEN media and right controls, current marker 980. Full-width black footer with skip and finish button. Small editorial rules and asymmetric baseline typography create dynamism. NO gratuitous diagonal shapes, no full neon background. Motion concept: active-set connector fills on completed set, numeral briefly scales subtly.'}
